WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.000
Welcome! Can you introduce yourself?

2
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.050
Hello! Thanks for having me today.

3
00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:09.850
My name is Sifeddine El Kadiri, a final-year student

4
00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.530
majoring in finance and computer science.

5
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.870
I’ve had many opportunities to do interviews with schools abroad

6
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.630
and with recruiting teams from different companies

7
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.080
when I was looking for a final-year internship.

8
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.340
And I’m here today to share my experience with you.

9
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:30.840
In our scene, Ayoub lists his strengths but gives a vague example.

10
00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:35.920
What do you think of his answer? And how would you improve it?

11
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.240
So I think Ayoub mentions good qualities,

12
00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:43.260
but he does not give the jury enough evidence.

13
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.080
Saying “I’ve done a lot of projects”

14
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.480
does not explain the challenges, his personal contribution or the results.

15
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.500
For my interviews, I prepared examples from university projects.

16
00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.100
I organised each answer into four parts:

17
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:03.120
the situation, my responsibility, my actions and the results.

18
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.760
For instance, instead of simply saying “I am a good team player”,

19
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.860
you could say: “In a group project, we fell behind schedule.

20
00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.720
I was responsible for combining our work,

21
00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.720
so I organised a meeting to identify the problems and help resolve a technical issue.

22
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:20.740
We submitted our work and application on time.”

23
00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:24.860
In this example, the answer shows teamwork through specific actions.

24
00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.280
If you have an accurate number, include it.

25
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.320
But don’t invent it.

26
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.280
A clear outcome is useful too.

27
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.820
So finally, my advice to Ayoub would be to prepare a few honest examples.

28
00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.060
You don’t need years of experience.

29
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:43.080
A university project, a club activity or a volunteering experience

30
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.240
can demonstrate your strengths.

31
00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:51.710
Perfect. Thank you for sharing your experience and advice.

32
00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.920
You’re welcome. Thanks for having me today.
